{"created": "2025-06-15T15:09:54.489930+00:00", "modified": "2025-06-15T15:09:54.719217+00:00", "id": 15668685, "conceptrecid": "15668684", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15668685", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15668684", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15668685", "metadata": {"title": "TUC-RedTeam30: A Dataset for Evaluating ML-Based Network Intrusion Detection Systems", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15668685", "publication_date": "2025-06-15", "description": "<p><strong>TUC-RedTeam30 Dataset for NIDS Benchmarking</strong></p>\n<p>The Technical University of Chemnitz Red Team 30 (TUC-RedTeam30) dataset was collected during 30 distinct red teaming exercises conducted in a controlled and isolated environment. It is part of the artifact accompanying our USENIX WOOT'25 paper, <em>\"DeepRed: A Deep Learning&ndash;Powered Command and Control Framework for Multi-Stage Red Teaming Against ML-based Network Intrusion Detection Systems.\"</em></p>\n<p>Each scenario in the dataset represents a unique red team engagement and benign traffic (Web, Email, DNS, Streaming etc.),&nbsp; specifically designed to evaluate and challenge both signature-based and machine learning&ndash;based Network Intrusion Detection Systems (NIDS). Detailed descriptions of the 30 scenarios mapped to MITRE ATT&amp;ck framework are provided in Appendix A of the main paper.</p>\n<p><strong>Data Formats</strong><br>The dataset is provided in two formats, both compressed using tar.gz (no password protection):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CSV Format: Contains labeled traffic flow features extracted from all PCAP files for 30 scenarios using the NFStream tool. The features across all scenarios have been combined into a single file for streamlined analysis. Each flow record is annotated with labels and metadata (scenario number).</li>\n<li>Label \"0\" denotes benign (normal) activity, while label \"1\" indicates malicious activity.</li>\n<li>PCAP Format: Due to the large size of the raw PCAP files, only a representative subset is included in this release. These PCAPs correspond to selected scenarios and are suitable for deeper packet-level analysis and feature extraction.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Information</strong></p>\n<p>For detailed information on malicious IP addresses, ports, attack labeling, attack stages, tools used, and targets, please refer to Appendix A in the main paper.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Hajizadeh, Mehrdad", "affiliation": "Technische Universit\u00e4t Chemnitz", "orcid": "0009-0008-3375-0912"}, {"name": "Golchin, Pegah", "affiliation": "Technische Universit\u00e4t Chemnitz", "orcid": "0000-0002-8686-113X"}, {"name": "Nowroozi, Ehsan", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-5714-8378"}, {"name": "Rigaki, Maria", "affiliation": "Czech Technical University in Prague", "orcid": "0000-0002-0688-7752"}, {"name": "Valeros, Veronica", "affiliation": "Czech Technical University in Prague", "orcid": "0000-0003-2554-3231"}, {"name": "Garcia, Sebastian", "affiliation": "Czech Technical University in Prague", "orcid": "0000-0001-6238-9910"}, {"name": "Conti, Mauro", "affiliation": "University of Padua", "orcid": "0000-0002-3612-1934"}, {"name": "Bauschert, Thomas", "affiliation": "Technische Universit\u00e4t Chemnitz"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "meeting": {"title": "USENIX WOOT Conference on Offensive Technologies", "acronym": "USENIX WOOT'25", "dates": "11-12, August, 2025", "place": "Seattle, WA, USA", "url": "https://www.usenix.org/conference/woot25"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "15668684"}}]}}, "title": "TUC-RedTeam30: A Dataset for Evaluating ML-Based Network Intrusion Detection Systems", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15668685", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15668685", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15668685?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zeno